# The CORE-ET benchmark corpus: 122 modules.
#
# SCOPE, stated rather than implied. This is a CHOSEN SUBSET, not all of
# CORE-ET. The upstream inventory (`core_et_blocks.txt`) counts 215
# non-technology RTL modules on main -- module declarations under rtl/, with
# dv/ testbenches excluded -- plus 34 technology primitives, 249 distinct RTL
# modules in all. So every coverage fraction quoted against this file is "of
# the 122 we attempt", never "of CORE-ET".
#
# The rule that selected these 122 is NOT recorded anywhere, and this file does
# not reconstruct it. Only 48 of the 122 appear in the upstream inventory under
# the same name, so it is not a prefix of that list and the remainder are not
# accounted for here. Treat the set as declared, and say so when quoting a
# number from it.
#
# One list, two consumers: the D4/DCERT2 sweep and scripts/coverage_ledger.py.
# A second copy would be one more thing to drift.
